<title>TURKEY: Turk PM sees lira Jan devaluation not above 5 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk PM sees lira Jan devaluation not above 5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkish Prime Minister Necmettin Erbakan said the devaluation of the Turkish lira will not be above five percent in January and will subsequently fall to around four percent daily.</p>
<p>&quot;The value of the currency will not change this month by more than five percent. After that it will be falling around four percent (monthly),&quot; Erbakan told a meeting of his Islamist Welfare Party.</p>
</text>
